agent: **Here is a proposed starting point for your architecture:**
  **Title:** Restock Alerts
  **Summary:** A scheduled job reads current stock levels, identifies items at or below their reorder point, and sends one alert to the responsible person.
  **Applies:** Weekly restock-alert production and delivery.
  **Leaves open:** The alert channel and exact schedule.
  **Style:** Scheduled, read-oriented notification flow.
  **Why:** This removes the manual stock check while keeping stock access separate from payment data.
  **Components:**
  - **Scheduler:** Starts the weekly alert process. Interface: Provides a scheduled trigger.
  - **Stock Reader:** Retrieves stock levels and reorder points through a read-only interface. Interface: Returns stock data to the evaluator.
  - **Restock Evaluator:** Determines which items require attention. Interface: Produces a restock alert when thresholds are met.
  - **Alert Sender:** Delivers one alert to the responsible person. Interface: Accepts alert content and delivery destination.
  **Information:** Stock levels, reorder points, item identifiers, and alert details are handled by the job. The order service owns stock data; the alert flow owns generated alert content. Payment data must not cross into this flow.
  **Must keep:** Weekly scheduled execution, read-only stock access, one alert for qualifying items, and no payment-data access.
  **May choose:** Alert channel, exact schedule, and delivery implementation.
  **Responsibilities:**
  - Schedule and start the alert process.
  - Read current stock levels and reorder points.
  - Identify items requiring restock.
  - Deliver one alert.
  - Assign ownership for failed runs.
  - Exclude payment data.
  **Interactions:** The Scheduler invokes the Stock Reader. The Stock Reader supplies data to the Restock Evaluator. The Evaluator sends qualifying results to the Alert Sender.
  **Trust boundaries:** The order service remains responsible for stock data. The alert flow may read stock data but may not access payment data. The alert recipient is responsible for acting on delivered alerts.
  **Deployment:** A separately operated scheduled job with observable run outcomes and an assigned failure owner.
  **Constraints:** No new paid vendors. Support one-day shipping. Follow the payment-data protection control. Depend on the order service availability requirement.
  **Risks:** A failed or unnoticed run can delay alerts for up to a week. The stock query has not been load tested.
  **Capabilities:** Restock alert generation — Restock Evaluator.
  **What would you add, correct, or remove?**
  If this is accurate, just say so.
